  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1511,
      "versionNonce": 1368959420,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "UjqAlA1p15c_nKLkZGvPa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": -333.3664563747004,
      "y": -533.0280569853599,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 770,
      "height": 1500,
      "seed": 669618308,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782675898725,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Webhook\nFunctional Requirements\n- register events \n- send events\n- states of events\n- user can fetch registered webhooks \n\nNon Functional Requirements\n- availability >> consistency\n- Latency of sending events should be minimal ~1s\n- system should be reliable, means able to handle errors and  security\n- all events are durable\n- at least once delivery without duplication\n\nCore entities\n- Event - rules, name, id, etc.\n- States - Pending, COMPLETED, IN_PROGRESS, FAILED\n- RegisteredApplication - url, event names, etc.\n\nAPIs \n- POST\n/register\nheaders:\ntoken: \nrequest:\n- event_name\n- target_url\n- client_id\nresponse:\n201OK- created\n\n- POST\n/send\nheaders\ntoken: <CLIENT_ID>\nrequest:\nidemp_key: <> //github-123, amazon-123\npayload: {\n\n}\nevent_name: \nresponse:\n200OK - event_id\n\nGET /status?event_id=$\nheaders - token: <CLIENT_ID>\n200 OK - status\n\nGET /webhooks\nheaders: token: <CLIENT_ID>\nresponse\nwebhook:\n    events:[{event_name: , event_ids:[], ....}]\n\nSCALE:\n100k/s send events => 4x peak = 400k/s\n\nHLD:\n\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Webhook\nFunctional Requirements\n- register events \n- send events\n- states of events\n- user can fetch registered webhooks \n\nNon Functional Requirements\n- availability >> consistency\n- Latency of sending events should be minimal ~1s\n- system should be reliable, means able to handle errors and  security\n- all events are durable\n- at least once delivery without duplication\n\nCore entities\n- Event - rules, name, id, etc.\n- States - Pending, COMPLETED, IN_PROGRESS, FAILED\n- RegisteredApplication - url, event names, etc.\n\nAPIs \n- POST\n/register\nheaders:\ntoken: \nrequest:\n- event_name\n- target_url\n- client_id\nresponse:\n201OK- created\n\n- POST\n/send\nheaders\ntoken: <CLIENT_ID>\nrequest:\nidemp_key: <> //github-123, amazon-123\npayload: {\n\n}\nevent_name: \nresponse:\n200OK - event_id\n\nGET /status?event_id=$\nheaders - token: <CLIENT_ID>\n200 OK - status\n\nGET /webhooks\nheaders: token: <CLIENT_ID>\nresponse\nwebhook:\n    events:[{event_name: , event_ids:[], ....}]\n\nSCALE:\n100k/s send events => 4x peak = 400k/s\n\nHLD:\n\n",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 1476
    },
